**Goal Model – Multi‑Robot Resource Collection & Delivery**

| Goal ID | Goal Title | Text | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
|---------|------------|------|--------------------|-----------|----------|
| G1 | Deliver Requested Resources | Ensure the requested resources are collected from the storage places and delivered to the requesting agent at the specified location. | # | Perform | - |
| G1.1 | Collect‑Deliver Resource R1 | Perform a full collect‑deliver cycle for one required resource (R1). | ; | Perform | AND |
| G1.1.1 | Collection Phase for R1 | Collect the resource from the appropriate storage place following the estimated order. | ; | Perform | AND |
| G1.1.1.1 | Determine Order of Storage Visits | Retrieve and compute the best visiting order based on waiting times and path lengths. | - | Query | AND |
| G1.1.1.2 | Go to Storage Place | Navigate to the next storage location in the determined order. | - | Perform | AND |
| G1.1.1.3 | Request Resource | Send a message to the storage with the exact specification of the requested resource. | - | Perform | AND |
| G1.1.1.4 | Wait for Retrieval | Await the confirmation that the resource has been retrieved. | - | Perform | AND |
| G1.1.1.5 | Monitor Battery in Collection | Check the battery level during the collection phase. | FALLBACK(GoToRechargeAndAssignMission, ContinueCollection) | Perform | AND |
| G1.1.1.5.1 | Go to Recharge & Assign Mission | If battery <10 %, go to the recharging station and delegate the remaining mission to another robot. | - | Perform | AND |
| G1.1.2 | Delivery Phase for R1 | Deliver the collected resource to the specified destination. | ; | Perform | AND |
| G1.1.2.1 | Navigate to Destination | Move to the destination location where the resource must be delivered. | - | Perform | AND |
| G1.1.2.2 | Deliver Resource | Transfer the resource to the requesting agent at the destination. | - | Perform | AND |
| G1.1.2.3 | Monitor Battery in Delivery | Check the battery level during the delivery phase. | FALLBACK(ReturnResourceCheckpointAssignOther, ContinueDelivery) | Perform | AND |
| G1.1.2.3.1 | Return Resource to Checkpoint | If battery <30 %, return the resource to a checkpoint. | - | Perform | AND |
| G1.1.2.3.2 | Assign Remaining Task to Another Robot | After returning the resource, delegate the remaining delivery tasks to another robot. | - | Perform | AND |
| G1.1.2.4 | Handle Failure to Return | If the resource cannot be returned to the checkpoint, trigger an alert and report to the sector manager. | - | Perform | AND |

